      "reason": "Adopt server-native thread working directories in the app-server API. Keep the fork\u2019s runtime version, session identity and retained local execution binding. Convert paths at the API or local filesystem boundary using upstream types.",
      "evidence": [
        "The preceding 0.12 CLI at e317f1333a on Unix completed a real remote exec turn with the server\u2019s Unix cwd. Both exec and exec resume failed to decode otherwise valid replies carrying a Windows drive path, before sending turn/start. The seed thread came from the same real server and its provider was loopback.",
        "Upstream uses LegacyAppPathString for the wire path and PathUri under the server convention inside the TUI. The app-server rejects a non-UTF-8 native path when emitting the current settings. The JSON field remains a string.",
        "The fork changes session model and history projection, runtime version reporting and local ownership at these sites. Preserve those hooks, use the server\u2019s API conversion for retained task creation and its Daybreak config lookup, and keep the same original runtime when projecting a resumed session."
      ],
      "revisit": "Run protocol response round trips, non-UTF-8 rejection, remote diff and project-title tests, then repeat the recorded Unix client / Windows server-path experiment for both start and resume on the merged executable. Recheck local retained UI and saved model continuation."
